@@ -345,3 +345,26 @@
 .. click:run::
     invoke(cli, ['-h'])
 ```
+
+## Custom Help Formatters
+
+Help pages are written by a {class}`HelpFormatter`. The class and the helpers it lays out text with (`wrap_text`,
+`measure_table`, `iter_rows`) live in the module `click._help_formatter`; `click.HelpFormatter` and the names in
+`click.formatting` are the same objects, so code that imports them from either place keeps working. To change how help
+pages look, subclass the formatter and set it as the context's `formatter_class`:
+
+```python
+class WideFormatter(click.HelpFormatter):
+    def write_dl(self, rows, col_max=40, col_spacing=4):
+        super().write_dl(rows, col_max, col_spacing)
+
+class WideContext(click.Context):
+    formatter_class = WideFormatter
+
+@click.command()
+@click.option("--name", help="The name.")
+def hello(name):
+    pass
+
+hello.context_class = WideContext
+```
